## Module 0 — WL Basics for Math

Three things you'll use constantly:
- `=` sets a variable, `:=` defines a function (delayed evaluation)
- `Plot`, `Manipulate` for visualization
- `N[...]` forces a numeric approximation; without it, WL keeps exact/symbolic results

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Module 0 — WL Basics for Math

Three things you'll use constantly:
- `=` sets a variable, `:=` defines a function (delayed evaluation)
- `Plot`, `Manipulate` for visualization
- `N[...]` forces a numeric approximation; without it, WL keeps exact/symbolic results

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(* setup: readable numeric output — 2 decimals by default *)
(* WLJS bypasses the kernel main loop, so $Post/$Pre/$PrePrint do nothing. *)
(* Apply explicitly with  expr // fmt  or  fmt[expr, n]  for n decimals.   *)
ClearAll[fmt];
fmt[expr_, n_Integer: 2] := expr /. {
  z_Complex :> N[Round[Re[z], 10^-n]] + I*N[Round[Im[z], 10^-n]],
  x_Real :> Which[
    x == 0., 0.,
    Abs[x] >= 10^-n, N[Round[x, 10^-n]],
    True, N[Round[x, 10^(Floor[Log10[Abs[x]]] - 1)]]   (* 2 sig digits, never 0. *)
  ]
};

(* pp: pretty-print a list of  "label" -> value  rules as an aligned table *)
(* Apply with  {...} // pp   or  pp[{...}, n]  for n decimals.             *)
ClearAll[pp];
pp[rules : {__Rule}, n_Integer: 2] := Grid[
  {Style[First[#], Bold], fmt[Last[#], n]} & /@ rules,
  Alignment -> {{Left, Right}}, Spacings -> {3, 1},
  Dividers -> {False, {False, {Directive[LightGray, Thin]}, False}}];

{Pi, 1/3, N[Pi], 0.00012345, 1.23456 + 7.89012 I} // fmt

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
{\[Pi],(*FB[*)((1)(*,*)/(*,*)(3))(*]FB*),3.14`,0.00012`,1.23` +7.89` I}

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(* same data, four renderings - pick the one you like and we standardise on it *)
demo = {"price at r = 4%"        -> price[0.04],
        "dP/dr (dollar duration)" -> price'[0.04],
        "modified duration"       -> -price'[0.04]/price[0.04],
        "convexity"               -> price''[0.04]/price[0.04],
        "P&L for a +1bp move"     -> price'[0.04]*0.0001};

Column[{
  Style["1. raw  (what we have now)", Bold, Darker[Red]],
  demo // fmt[#, 4] &,

  Style["2. pp  ->  Grid, aligned + ruled", Bold, Darker[Green]],
  pp[demo, 4],

  Style["3. TableForm with headings", Bold, Darker[Blue]],
  TableForm[List @@@ (demo /. Rule[k_, v_] :> Rule[k, fmt[v, 4]]),
    TableHeadings -> {None, {"quantity", "value"}}],

  Style["4. Dataset", Bold, Darker[Magenta]],
  Dataset[Association @@ (demo /. Rule[k_, v_] :> Rule[k, fmt[v, 4]])]
}, Spacings -> 1.5]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
