%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
### Optimization

At a smooth peak or valley the tangent is flat, so $f'(x)=0$. Solving that gives **critical points**; the second derivative then says which is which:

- $f''>0$ → curve bends up → **local minimum**
- $f''<0$ → curve bends down → **local maximum**
- $f''=0$ → inconclusive, need more care

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
### Optimization

At a smooth peak or valley the tangent is flat, so $f'(x)=0$. Solving that gives **critical points**; the second derivative then says which is which:

- $f''>0$ → curve bends up → **local minimum**
- $f''<0$ → curve bends down → **local maximum**
- $f''=0$ → inconclusive, need more care

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(* find critical points, then classify them with the second derivative *)
crit = x /. Solve[g'[x] == 0, x];

TableForm[
  Table[{xc, g[xc], g''[xc],
     Which[g''[xc] > 0, "local min", g''[xc] < 0, "local max", True, "inconclusive"]},
    {xc, crit}],
  TableHeadings -> {None, {"x*", "g(x*)", "g''(x*)", "type"}}
]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*GB[*){{"x*"(*|*),(*|*)"g(x*)"(*|*),(*|*)"g''(x*)"(*|*),(*|*)"type"}(*||*),(*||*){1(*|*),(*|*)5(*|*),(*|*)-6(*|*),(*|*)"local max"}(*||*),(*||*){3(*|*),(*|*)1(*|*),(*|*)6(*|*),(*|*)"local min"}}(*||*)(*1:eJyNj8EOgjAMhqfR6MXoK/goIsGLJzDeJ3SkydjMCuLju4EGB1nCZfn791v/9vjQqVgxxmhnnztCG0OuDa+1yZx9MViIpeu7Km0k0P5rR/od4wsLMDQQV6Ta57ONFWctm0qRWHicV9HaioRLgtH/TuiW+jWneGfdTAOheaHJ/5dkT56jKmdfgi4rsCiySY8OQ9RJYqkqUPXcrB4BMUZ+ebS1IuIEEhV8ACxVZkc=*)(*]GB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: false
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(* f, f' and f'' stacked - one slider morphs through ALL THREE cases *)
(*   k > 0  : two critical points, a max on the left and a min on the right *)
(*   k = 0  : they merge - f'=0 AND f''=0, so the test gives no answer      *)
(*   k < 0  : no critical points at all, f just climbs                      *)
ClearAll[critPts, kind, critLabel];

critPts[k_] := Which[k > 0.0005, {-Sqrt[k], Sqrt[k]}, Abs[k] <= 0.0005, {0.}, True, {}];
kind[xc_]   := Which[6 xc > 0.001, "local min", 6 xc < -0.001, "local max", True, "INCONCLUSIVE"];
critLabel[k_] := If[critPts[k] === {},
   "no critical points - f is strictly increasing",
   StringRiffle[MapThread[
     "x = " <> ToString[NumberForm[#1, {3, 2}]] <> "  ->  " <> #2 &,
     {critPts[k], kind /@ critPts[k]}], "       "]];

Manipulate[
  Column[{
    Show[
      Plot[x^3 - 3 k x, {x, -3, 3}, PlotRange -> {-12, 12}, ImageSize -> 430,
        PlotLabel -> critLabel[k]],
      Graphics[{Red, PointSize[0.022], Point[{#, #^3 - 3 k #}] & /@ critPts[k]}]],

    Show[
      Plot[3 x^2 - 3 k, {x, -3, 3}, PlotRange -> {-12, 20}, ImageSize -> 430,
        PlotLabel -> "f'(x)  -  crosses zero exactly at the critical points",
        Epilog -> {Gray, Dashed, Line[{{-3, 0}, {3, 0}}]}],
      Graphics[{Red, PointSize[0.022], Point[{#, 0}] & /@ critPts[k]}]],

    Show[
      Plot[6 x, {x, -3, 3}, PlotRange -> {-20, 20}, ImageSize -> 430,
        PlotLabel -> "f''(x)  -  its SIGN is what classifies each one",
        Epilog -> {Gray, Dashed, Line[{{-3, 0}, {3, 0}}]}],
      Graphics[{Red, PointSize[0.022], Point[{#, 6 #}] & /@ critPts[k]}]]
  }],
  {{k, 1, "k"}, -1, 3, 0.05},
  ContinuousAction -> True
]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
